meta {
  name: tag: overleaf (stack)
  type: http
  seq: 22
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/pods/templates/overleaf/tags
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  X-Tapis-Token: {{X-Tapis-Token}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "kind": "stack",
    "stack_definition": {
      "restart_policy": "ordered",
      "members": [
        {
          "name": "mongo",
          "image": "mongo:6",
          "description": "MongoDB 6 for Overleaf CE. MUST run as a single-node replica set (Overleaf >= 4 requires it). Replica set needs a one-time rs.initiate() - see docs.",
          "arguments": ["mongod", "--replSet", "overleaf", "--bind_ip_all"],
          "ready_condition": "ready",
          "time_to_stop_default": -1,
          "networking": {
            "default": { "protocol": "local_only", "port": 27017, "tapis_auth": false }
          },
          "healthchecks": {
            "readiness": {
              "exec_command": ["mongosh", "--quiet", "--eval", "db.adminCommand('ping').ok"],
              "initial_delay_seconds": 10,
              "period_seconds": 10
            },
            "networking_requires_ready": false
          },
          "resources": { "cpu_request": 250, "cpu_limit": 2000, "mem_request": 512, "mem_limit": 2048 }
        },
        {
          "name": "redis",
          "image": "redis:7-alpine",
          "description": "Redis 7 for Overleaf real-time/session state. local_only.",
          "ready_condition": "ready",
          "time_to_stop_default": -1,
          "networking": {
            "default": { "protocol": "local_only", "port": 6379, "tapis_auth": false }
          },
          "healthchecks": {
            "readiness": {
              "exec_command": ["redis-cli", "ping"],
              "initial_delay_seconds": 3,
              "period_seconds": 5
            },
            "networking_requires_ready": false
          },
          "resources": { "cpu_request": 100, "cpu_limit": 1000, "mem_request": 128, "mem_limit": 1024 }
        },
        {
          "name": "sharelatex",
          "image": "sharelatex/sharelatex:latest",
          "description": "Overleaf Community Edition web app + compiler. Connects to the in-stack mongo (directConnection - single-node RS) and redis.",
          "depends_on": ["mongo", "redis"],
          "ready_condition": "available",
          "time_to_stop_default": -1,
          "environment_variables": {
            "SHARELATEX_MONGO_URL": "mongodb://${stack:mongo:host}/sharelatex?directConnection=true",
            "SHARELATEX_REDIS_HOST": "${stack:redis:host}",
            "REDIS_HOST": "${stack:redis:host}",
            "SHARELATEX_APP_NAME": "Overleaf (self-hosted)",
            "SHARELATEX_SITE_URL": "${:?Public site URL, e.g. https://myoverleaf.pods.<base> - Overleaf bakes this into links/PDF downloads}",
            "ENABLED_LINKED_FILE_TYPES": "project_file,project_output_file",
            "ENABLE_CONVERSIONS": "true"
          },
          "networking": {
            "default": {
              "protocol": "http",
              "port": 80,
              "tapis_auth": true,
              "tapis_auth_allowed_users": ["*"],
              "tapis_auth_return_path": "/launchpad",
              "tapis_ui_uri_redirect": true,
              "tapis_ui_uri_description": "Overleaf CE - first visit /launchpad to create the admin user"
            }
          },
          "healthchecks": {
            "readiness": {
              "http_get_path": "/status",
              "http_get_port": 80,
              "initial_delay_seconds": 30,
              "period_seconds": 15,
              "failure_threshold": 8
            }
          },
          "resources": { "cpu_request": 1000, "cpu_limit": 4000, "mem_request": 2048, "mem_limit": 8192 },
          "compute_queue": "default"
        }
      ]
    },
    "tag": "ce-stack-experimental",
    "commit_message": "Overleaf Community Edition stack: sharelatex + mongo (single-node replSet) + redis. EXPERIMENTAL - requires a one-time mongo rs.initiate() and TeX Live install; see docs."
  }
}

docs {
  ## Overleaf / self-hosted LaTeX - yes, with caveats

  **Can you self-host Overleaf? Yes** - Overleaf **Community Edition** (`sharelatex/sharelatex`) is
  the open-source release of overleaf.com and is the standard way to self-host a collaborative
  LaTeX editor. It is **not single-container**: it needs **3 containers** - the app + **MongoDB** +
  **Redis**. This stack wires those together.

  ### LaTeX editors "in general"
  Overleaf CE is the only mature, browser-based, multi-user LaTeX editor you can self-host. Lighter
  options exist but trade features: TeXLive + a generic IDE pod (code-server with a LaTeX
  extension - see the `codeserver` tags) for single-user editing, or a plain JupyterLab pod for
  quick `.tex` compiles. If you want the real Overleaf collaborative experience, this stack is it.

  ### Why "EXPERIMENTAL" - two things this stack can't fully automate
  1. **Mongo must be a single-node replica set** (Overleaf >= 4 requirement). The member starts
     `mongod --replSet overleaf`, but a replica set needs a **one-time** init that can't be
     expressed declaratively. After the stack is up, exec into the mongo pod once:
     ```
     mongosh --eval 'rs.initiate({_id:"overleaf",members:[{_id:0,host:"127.0.0.1:27017"}]})'
     ```
     (Use the Pods exec tab, or `kubectl exec`.) The `?directConnection=true` on the app's
     `SHARELATEX_MONGO_URL` is what lets it talk to that single-node RS. Until you initiate,
     sharelatex's readiness probe (`/status`) will keep failing - that's expected.
  2. **TeX Live** - the base `sharelatex/sharelatex` image ships a *minimal* TeX Live. Real
     documents need more packages: exec in and run `tlmgr install scheme-full` (large, slow) or
     install the specific packages your docs use. Without this, compiles fail with "package not
     found".

  ### First run
  `POST /pods/stacks/from-template` with
  `{ "template": "overleaf:ce-stack-experimental", "stack_id": "myoverleaf",
     "pod_ids": { "sharelatex": "myoverleaf" },
     "overrides": { "sharelatex": { "environment_variables": {
       "SHARELATEX_SITE_URL": "https://myoverleaf.pods.<base>" } } } }`
  then: (1) `rs.initiate()` on mongo, (2) open `myoverleaf.pods.<base>/launchpad` to create the
  admin user, (3) `tlmgr install ...` as needed.

  > CE omits some overleaf.com Pro features (Git integration, SAML/LDAP, track-changes, advanced
  > collab limits). Give the app real memory (8 GB limit here) - LaTeX compiles are hungry. Pin
  > `sharelatex/sharelatex:latest` to a concrete version for anything you care about.
}
